## 6. RISK-036 probe (test-only uvicorn processes on this 2-cpu host; the load generator SHARES the host — scaling numbers are NOT capacity)
# server_cpu_cores = (utime+stime of the uvicorn process tree)/elapsed. 1 worker pins ≈1.0 core ⇒ the one-process ceiling is MEASURED, not inferred.
# with 2 workers the host is saturated by generator+server, so no throughput gain is visible here — a scaling measurement needs a separate generator (Q-023).
